@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-PERSIST-001 STRUCTURAL ANALYSIS PERSISTENCE (ADR-048). The exact
rem invocation, recorded so the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-EIGHT in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing -- same sources, same
rem flags, -Werror included. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THE AUDIT FOUND, AND WHY THIS MILESTONE IS ONE FILE. Every
rem architectural question the brief raises already had an answer in the tree
rem with a recorded reason: the file format, the version rule
rem (P13-PERSIST-001: bump only for a change an existing reader would get
rem WRONG), the unknown-field policy (requireObject rejects by allow-list),
rem the face-reference encoding (faceNameToJson, shared with six other object
rem kinds), atomic save, the save-failure path (objectToJson has always
rem returned Result<Json>), the derived-state argument (P16-PERSIST-001),
rem string enum keys from a table, and arrays rather than objects keyed by id.
rem
rem SO THIS RUN ADDS ONE OBJECT TYPE TO THE EXISTING FORMAT. No second file,
rem no version bump, no migration code, no new validation framework, no new
rem reference encoding and no new determinism mechanism.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED SINCE bde6f8b.
rem
rem   NEW          src/io/json/StructuralAnalysisJson.cpp
rem                               The serializer pair. 13 named helpers, four
rem                               constexpr name tables, no map, no hash and
rem                               no sort.
rem                tests/io/StructuralAnalysisFileTests.cpp
rem                               38 cases, 40 sections.
rem                examples/models/analysed_plate.bcad
rem                               A hand-written document, read by two tests:
rem                               one checks every field as written, the other
rem                               regenerates, meshes and SOLVES it.
rem
rem   MODIFIED     src/io/json/ObjectJson.hpp
rem                               One include and two declarations, beside
rem                               every other object kind's pair.
rem                src/io/json/DocumentJson.cpp
rem                               Two dispatch branches. The writer branch is
rem                               the only one in the format that can FAIL, so
rem                               it propagates a Result rather than assigning.
rem                src/io/CMakeLists.txt
rem                               One source, one PRIVATE_LINK on
rem                               BetterCAD::structural. io is layer 60 and
rem                               structural is 50, so the edge points down.
rem                tests/CMakeLists.txt
rem                               One source.
rem
rem NO STRUCTURAL PRODUCTION FILE CHANGED -- not one. So NO P17 PREDECESSOR IS
rem REQUALIFIED BY THIS RUN, which is the opposite of P17-CMD-001, where four
rem were. The blast radius is io: the whole document-persistence suite, which
rem every preset runs unfiltered.
rem
rem THE ONE GENUINELY NEW DECISION: A NODAL FORCE LOAD REFUSES THE SAVE.
rem NodalForceLoad is the only canonical payload holding mesh-local state, a
rem MeshStamp and a NodeId. ADR-031 says those are "never persisted",
rem P17-LOAD-001 declares the type mesh-local and explicitly "NOT durable
rem point-load intent on the model", and the brief lists a persisted NodeId as
rem an automatic failure. All three AGREE, so there was no conflict to resolve
rem -- only a consequence to choose, from four candidates. Writing it would
rem store a load that no reload could ever resolve, because the stamp names a
rem mesh generation that cannot exist again. Writing it WITHOUT the stamp is
rem the forbidden rebind, in the mesh dimension. Dropping it is silent data
rem loss. So the save is refused, atomically, naming the load.
rem
rem AND THE COST WAS MEASURED RATHER THAN ESTIMATED: NodalForceLoad has ZERO
rem callers in apps/ and zero in src/ outside its own definition. It exists
rem only in tests, which is exactly what P17-LOAD-001 said it was for -- so the
rem refusal guards a path that does not exist yet, which is the cheapest moment
rem to put a guard in.
rem
rem THE HARD GATE IS BYTE IDENTITY ACROSS THE SOLVE, and it compares FOUR
rem states rather than two, because a format that wrote a result only when the
rem result was VALID would pass a before/after comparison: no result at all, a
rem CURRENT result, a STALE one (reached by remeshing, which touches no
rem document object) and one after a FAILED solve. All four measured at 4426
rem bytes and compared BYTE FOR BYTE, not by size. The structural section is
rem also identical across a 499-element and a 1313-element mesh, at 907 bytes.
rem
rem TWO CLAIMS ARE SIGNATURES RATHER THAN TESTS, which is stronger. The writer
rem takes only the document object and a StructuralResult does not live on one,
rem so there is no expression it could write that depends on whether a solve
rem has run. The reader takes a Json, a name and a path -- no Document, no
rem Regenerator, no Mesher, no geometry -- so there is nothing for an
rem unresolved reference to be rebound TO. Both were MEASURED: two of the
rem brief's requested mutations could not be written at all, and MUTATION.md
rem records them as unreachable rather than as probes that passed.
rem
rem MUTATION: the probes ran BEFORE this qualification, not after it, and a
rem surviving probe would have stopped the pre-freeze gates by design rather
rem than being discovered inside a three-hour run.
rem
rem ADVERSARIAL REVIEW: 33 attacks from the brief's own list, 13 findings, 0
rem production defects. Six were found by READING and seven by a test FAILING,
rem and the two sets are disjoint. Three are worth naming here because they
rem were my own errors and the evidence records them rather than tidying them
rem away: I used a BLOCK to test mesh refinement, which cannot work because a
rem block's boundary is exactly representable so 20mm and 5mm give the same 24
rem tetrahedra -- P16 recorded that three times and it was in my own notes; I
rem wrote a comment claiming validate(StructuralLoad) is what refuses 1e999
rem when the PARSER refuses it first, which P16 had also already recorded; and
rem two of my own assertions were weak, using `!= Accepted` to mean "the solve
rem must not proceed" when AcceptedWithWarnings does proceed.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED:
rem `unit\.Structural` already covers unit.StructuralPersistence as a
rem substring, so the 38 new cases join the repeat set without touching the
rem filter. The SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS RUN rather than predicted
rem here -- a figure nobody has measured does not belong in the evidence for a
rem run.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem fifteen milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating
rem one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still run
rem UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
